{"name":"Alpine Duck Grey","hex":"#40464d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alpine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or inhabiting mountains, especially above the timberline.","Alternative letter-case form of Alpine: Of, relating to, or inhabiting the Alps, a large mountain range in Europe."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants, native to mountain habitats, often grown in rock gardens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alpine"},{"term":"duck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To quickly lower (the head or body), often in order to prevent it from being struck by something.","To lower (something) into water; to thrust or plunge under liquid and suddenly withdraw."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cave passage containing water with low, or no, airspace."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duck","blocks":[{"text":"Duck is the common name for numerous species of waterfowl in the family Anatidae. Ducks are generally smaller and shorter-necked than swans and geese, which are members of the same family. Divided among several subfamilies, they are a form taxon; they do not represent a monophyletic group, since swans and geese are not considered ducks. Ducks are mostly aquatic birds, and may be found in both fresh water and sea water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg/330px-Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is a